commit 8916b37f14ab01e6463144109acd59a1e5f2783f
Author: Anton Marini <vade@vade.info>
Date:   Mon Jan 26 18:53:52 2026 -0500

    Feature/vlm external video frames support [Draft] (#64)
    
    * Sketch converting an input array of VideoFrames into a ProcessedFrames via a new asProcessedSequence function
    
    * Placeholder updates to UserInput (commented out) to think about how we need to change asset handling? Commiting only as a way to start discussion
    
    * Fix compilation / overzealous in progress commenting.
    
    * Promote VideoFrame to UserInput
    
    * Update SmolVLM2
    
    * Update Qwen2VL
    
    * Update Quen25VL
    
    * Update Qwen3VL
    
    * Add typealias and remove API break at some call sites.
    
    * Refactor implementation of asProcessedSequence to have a singular public call site, and ensure cases for asset, url and frames are handled. We additionally add some defensive checks for our asset, does it have a video track, and is it decodable.
    
    * mark asAVAsset() as deprecated, fatalError on accessing asset with VideoFrames
    
    * Fix bug where i was not sampling the video frames for the times correctly
    
    * Refactor our private methods to not break external clients but mark as deprecated in a clean way. Add an additional entrypoint to asProcessedSequence for client who whish to specify samples per second.
    
    * Add Resources to swift package for MediaProcessinfg Tests, add small movie and audio only file for our tests.
    
    * we need to ensure our ProcessedFrames has public accessors so we can validate in tests.

